From: Catalyst Linux
Subject: [PATCH] flash attention over the audio encoded, not up to 256 past it

With flash attention (on by default) the encoder's self-attention and the
decoder's cross-attention read their keys and values in a span rounded up
to 256 positions, and attend to all of it with no mask, though only
n_ctx positions were written. The rest is whatever an earlier run left
there: zeros at first, then keys and values of other audio. With the whole
30 s window (1500) that is 36 positions of zeros; with a shorter audio_ctx
(how the shell keeps the cost to the length of what was said) it is up to
255 positions of someone else's speech, and the same clip came back worded
differently from one request to the next.

The round-up is for GPU kernels, which this build has none of: the CPU's
flash attention takes any length. So the span is exactly what was encoded.
Measured on 74 LibriSpeech clips and JFK's: every request answered the same
way twice over, and with audio_ctx at the clip's length plus 128 (at least
320), 9.6% of words wrong against 9.4% for the whole 30 s window.

--- a/src/whisper.cpp
+++ b/src/whisper.cpp
@@ -2094,7 +2094,7 @@
 
     WHISPER_ASSERT(!!kv_pad.buffer);
 
-    const int n_ctx_pad = GGML_PAD(n_ctx, 256);
+    const int n_ctx_pad = n_ctx;
 
     struct ggml_init_params params = {
         /*.mem_size   =*/ wstate.sched_encode.meta.size(),
@@ -2323,7 +2323,7 @@
 
     const int n_state_head = n_state/n_head;
 
-    const int n_ctx_pad = GGML_PAD(n_ctx, 256);
+    const int n_ctx_pad = n_ctx;
 
     struct ggml_init_params params = {
         /*.mem_size   =*/ wstate.sched_cross.meta.size(),
@@ -2541,7 +2541,7 @@
     const int n_tokens    = batch.n_tokens;
     const int n_audio_ctx = wstate.exp_n_audio_ctx > 0 ? wstate.exp_n_audio_ctx : hparams.n_audio_ctx;
 
-    const int n_audio_ctx_pad = GGML_PAD(n_audio_ctx, 256);
+    const int n_audio_ctx_pad = n_audio_ctx;
 
     const int32_t n_kv    = worst_case ? n_ctx            : kv_self.n;
     const int32_t kv_head = worst_case ? n_ctx - n_tokens : kv_self.head;
